{
  "schema": 1,
  "name": "Highest Order raises Shadowsong's Mandate's Warden's Blade chance by 60 (#949)",
  "contract": "Highest Order 680771 (Spell.dbc, SpellFamilyName 32) carries E0 SPELL_AURA_ADD_PCT_MODIFIER (108, -25) on the cooldown and E1 SPELL_AURA_ADD_FLAT_MODIFIER (107) on SPELLMOD_CHANCE_OF_SUCCESS (18) with EffectBasePoints 59 (+60), both with EffectSpellClassMask word2 0x20, the SpellFamilyFlags word2 of Shadowsong's Mandate 805439 alone (flags [0,0,0x20]). Its description promises to raise the chance to trigger Warden's Blade by that amount; Mandate's own ProcChance is 40 (starcaller warden-1 report, DBC read), so 40+60 must reach 100%. Mandate's proc is the aura_ascension_starcaller_event script (AscensionStarcallerEvents.cpp): Check() requires an outgoing critical damage hit and then rolled Chance(player, 805439), which read the raw ProcChance and never applied SPELLMOD_CHANCE_OF_SUCCESS, so the talent was inert; Proc() then casts the highest known Warden's Blade 805508 on the target. Chance() now applies the modifier, and rev_20260921_10 sets spell_proc.Chance to 100 so the script roll is the only roll (Aura::CalcProcChance would otherwise roll the DBC chance a second time, giving 0.4 x 0.4 = 16% without the talent). Both fixtures are identical (race 1, class 26, level 80, 10000 melee hit and crit rating, so a Celestial Strike 800496 - SPELL_DAMAGE_CLASS_MELEE, instant, no cooldown - always hits and always crits, clamped at 100%) and each is given Mandate 805439 by set_aura, re-applied every five casts because its duration is 10 s. The new spell_cast_count metric counts casts of 805508 by the actor including the triggered ones; nobody casts Blade by hand, so every count is a Mandate proc. Twenty crits per fixture: with the talent the chance is 100% so the count reaches at least 16 (allowing four casts the server drops); before the fix it is 40%, and P(X>=16 of 20 at 0.4) = 0.03%. The control, without the talent, stays at 40% and must not exceed 14 (P(X>=15 of 20 at 0.4) = 0.16% false failure).",
